text:
sam: Heads-up — on very narrow viewports (<320px) the table becomes unusable: rows stack weirdly and action menus push content. I prototyped an alternative: switch to a stacked card list for ultra-narrow screens. Screenshot: https://img.redwood.dev/ux/stack-cards-prototype.png
alondra: Interesting. So instead of forcing the table to squeeze, we render each row as a compact card with primary/secondary fields stacked and a persistent "View details" CTA?
marco: That could solve wrapping and sticky header jumps. Cards can keep consistent heights and avoid horizontal scroll. But we need to consider density — cards show fewer rows per fold which affects power users.
tanvi: Tradeoff noted. Maybe only switch under 320px or when a user preference for "compact table" is off. Also add a toggle in settings to force table vs cards.
sam: Prototype CSS for switch: ```css
@media (max-width:320px){
  .table { display:none; }
  .table-as-cards { display:block; }
  .card { padding:12px; display:flex; justify-content:space-between; align-items:center; gap:8px; }
  .card .meta{flex:1; min-width:0}
}
```
alondra: Accessibility: cards need a clear focus order, each card should be a single interactive region with role="listitem" and the details CTA should be reachable by keyboard. Use aria-expanded for inline expansions.
marco: Also: if we use cards, ensure copy consistency: use "View details" (explicit) not "More". Hallway test: 15 folks — explicit copy wins. We should include that in the PR.
tanvi: Telemetry: measure conversion and task completion for card vs table: `ui.mobile.layout_variant = card|table` and `ui.mobile.card.opened`. We'll canary behind flag `mobile_stack_cards`.
ux-bot: Created issue https://github.com/redwood-inference/console/issues/3456 "stacked card fallback for ultra-narrow mobile" assigned to @alondra @marco.
sam: QA checklist: iPhone SE, older Android webviews, VoiceOver/TalkBack, keyboard-only focus, large fonts, RTL. Also measure perceived performance since more DOM nodes may be rendered. Consider virtualizing the card list.
design-bot: I've added mocks and an accessibility checklist in the PR draft https://github.com/redwood-inference/console/pull/3458. PR includes settings toggle, feature flag, and copy variations.
alondra: One more UX nit: when switching between table and cards during rotation, animate cross-fade to avoid layout jump. But respect reduced-motion.
marco: Agree. We'll implement a prefers-reduced-motion safe transition and test on low-end hardware.
sam: Great — I'll open a canary PR behind `mobile_stack_cards` and wire telemetry. Tagging @qa when ready. :rocket:
